<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seoul</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hanyang, Hanseong, Keijo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seoul is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, on the Han river in the north-west of the peninsula. As Hanyang, later Hanseong, it was the capital of Joseon from 1394, with palaces such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyeongbokgung">Gyeongbokgung</a>, and it remained the capital of the Korean Empire and, as Keijo, of Japanese-ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. Since 1948 it has been the capital of South Korea and one of the world's largest cities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seoul.jpg" alt="Seoul" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eunmi Park · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EC%A4%91%ED%99%94%EC%A0%84%EC%9D%98_%EB%82%AE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
